  "notes": "Select Harvests Limited (SHV) — ASX-listed almond grower / processor. Fiscal year ends 30 September; H1 ends 31 March. Owns and manages ~9,000 ha (~22.4K acres) of almond orchards (Robinvale Vic, Riverland SA, Wemen Vic) plus processing/marketing operation (insertion brand: Lucky, Sunsol, Renshaw etc., progressively divested in favour of bulk almond focus). Bearing trees / orchards are carried on book-cost basis (depreciated cost) under AASB116 — NOT fair value. Crop volume and pricing drive earnings; biological asset (almonds on tree) carried at FV at year-end. Highly cyclical: FY20-FY22 weak almond prices, FY23-FY25 recovery on tighter California crop. Reports almond crop in tonnes and average pool price A$/kg. Pre-2010 history: SHV was a much smaller snack-food + almond grower (Lucky, Sunsol, Nu-Vit brands) with ~2,000 ha orchards. FY10 transformative Timbercorp Almonds acquisition (~$100M, +6,000 ha) tripled scale and made SHV the largest listed almond grower in the southern hemisphere. Subsequent capital raises (FY15 Wemen, FY21, FY24) progressively scaled to ~9,000 ha. Pre-2010 figures from published Annual Reports; FY00–FY09 reported FY-only.",
